The display now always fits in 24 terminal rows and 80 columns, with tests that check it. All 22 tests pass (20 existing, 2 new).

The layout already added up to exactly 24 rows: the board with its top and bottom borders takes 22, then one status line and one controls line. The score, lines, level, next-piece preview and timer sit beside the board, so they add no rows. I made that a hard limit rather than something that only works because the numbers happen to add up:

- **`src/app.js`**: added constants for the 24-row, 80-column size and for the controls line. The screen is cut to 24 lines, and each line to 80 characters.
- **`src/renderer.js`**: the frame drawn to the terminal also stops at 24 lines, and no newline follows the last one, so the screen can't scroll.
- **`test/shell.test.js`**: one new test checks the screen while playing, while paused, with very large score, lines and time values, and on the game-over screen. Each time it checks for exactly 24 lines, no line over 80 characters, both borders, and the controls line. A second test checks that a 30-line frame is cut to 24 lines.

